+I migrated the template syntax from Jinja2 to Mako by replacing Jinja-style variable interpolation and control blocks with Mako’s `${...}` expressions and `%`-prefixed loop/conditional directives. The structure and content of the template remain the same.

+

+```python

+"""${name}.

+

+Parameters

+----------

+% for p in params:

+${p.argument} :${' ' + p.annotation if p.annotation else ''}

+    ${p.argument}

+% endfor

+% if return_type:

+Returns

+-------

+${return_type}

+

+% endif

+"""

+```
